    "facts": ["The Open RN text says it usually lasts under 6 months; the CDC 2022 guideline calls pain under 1 month acute and 1–3 months subacute.", "Often sharp and well localised, with stress signs such as a fast pulse, raised blood pressure and sweating.", "Treat with the least invasive drug that works; if an opioid is needed, use immediate-release at the lowest dose for the fewest days."],
