    "facts": ["Open RN uses longer than 6 months; IASP and the CDC 2022 guideline use longer than 3 months.", "Pain signals in the nervous system stay switched on. Vital signs are often normal, so a calm face does not mean no pain.", "Linked to arthritis, back pain, cancer, nerve pain, headache and fibromyalgia; often brings poor sleep, low mood and anxiety.", "CDC 2022: non-drug and non-opioid treatments are preferred; opioids only if the expected benefits outweigh the risks."],
    "life": "A man with knee osteoarthritis for 8 years uses exercise, weight loss, an NSAID gel and acetaminophen.",
