    "summary": "Pain caused by damage to, or disease of, the nerves themselves rather than ongoing tissue injury.",
    "facts": ["Described as burning, shooting, stabbing, tingling, pins and needles or electric shocks.", "Examples: diabetic neuropathy, post-herpetic neuralgia after shingles, sciatica, phantom limb pain.", "First-line drugs are adjuvants: gabapentin or pregabalin, tricyclics such as amitriptyline, SNRIs such as duloxetine, and topical lidocaine."],
    "life": "After shingles, an older woman feels burning pain where the rash was, even from the touch of her clothes.",
