    "facts": ["0 = no pain; 1–3 mild, 4–6 moderate, 7–10 severe.", "Pain is whatever the patient says it is: self-report is the most reliable measure. Also ask for their acceptable pain goal.", "FACES works from about age 3. For people who cannot self-report, use behaviour scales such as FLACC (young children) or PAINAD (dementia).", "Describe the pain fully with a mnemonic such as PQRSTU or OLDCARTS: onset, location, quality, severity, timing, what helps."],
